caso 130-todo-problema-tiene-nivel-conocido:
    fecha: "2026-09-28"
    origen:
        repo: "Fission-AI/OpenSpec"
        commit: "79b6aa9"
        cuando_utc: "2026-09-28T21:16:31+00:00"
        comando: "python3 sensor.py --openspec <@fission-ai/openspec 1.13.2>"
        evidencia_sha256: "sha256:65a0de3e0d0b97d87e16fb8335cf70577cbf7370cfc799db36ab3d2ac373c34a"
    procedencia: observada
    titulo: "openspec validate 1.13.2, corrido contra los fixtures que openspec.todo_problema_tiene_nivel_conocido nombra"
    etiqueta: verde_correcto
    sintoma:
        Ninguno: la CLI real cumple la cláusula de cli-validate que esta medida vuelve falsable.
    como_se_detecto: observacion
    medida: openspec.todo_problema_tiene_nivel_conocido
    evidencia:
        problema: caso, id, nivel, ruta, mensaje
            "cambio_sin_deltas#0", "ch", "ERROR", "file", "Change must have at least one delta. No deltas found. Ensure your change has a specs/ directory with capability folders (e.g. specs/http-server/spec.md) containing .md files that use delta headers (## ADDED/MODIFIED/REMOVED/RENAMED Requirements) and that each requirement includes at least one \"#### Scenario:\" block. If this change intentionally modifies no specs (pure refactor, tooling, docs), set \"skip_specs: true\" in the change's .openspec.yaml instead. Tip: run \"openspec change show <change-id> --json --deltas-only\" to inspect parsed deltas."
            "spec_sin_purpose#0", "cap", "ERROR", "file", "Spec must have a Purpose section. Missing required sections. Expected headers: \"## Purpose\" and \"## Requirements\". Example:\n## Purpose\n[brief purpose]\n\n## Requirements\n### Requirement: Clear requirement statement\nUsers SHALL ...\n\n#### Scenario: Descriptive name\n- **WHEN** ...\n- **THEN** ..."
            "requisito_sin_cuerpo#0", "cap", "ERROR", "requirements[0]", "Requirement \"Foo\" must contain SHALL or MUST"
            "escenarios_en_vinetas#0", "cap", "ERROR", "requirements.0.scenarios", "Requirement must have at least one scenario"
            "escenarios_en_vinetas#0", "cap", "WARNING", "requirements[0].scenarios", "Requirement must have at least one scenario. Scenarios must use level-4 headers. Convert bullet lists into:\n#### Scenario: Short name\n- **WHEN** ...\n- **THEN** ...\n- **AND** ..."
            "spec_sin_palabra_clave#0", "cap", "WARNING", "requirements[0]", "Requirement \"Foo\" should contain SHALL or MUST (RFC 2119 best practice for English specs)"
            "spec_sin_palabra_clave#1", "cap", "WARNING", "requirements[0]", "Requirement \"Foo\" should contain SHALL or MUST (RFC 2119 best practice for English specs)"
            "delta_sin_palabra_clave#0", "ch", "WARNING", "cap/spec.md", "ADDED \"Bar\" should contain SHALL or MUST (RFC 2119 best practice for English specs)"
            "delta_sin_palabra_clave#1", "ch", "WARNING", "cap/spec.md", "ADDED \"Bar\" should contain SHALL or MUST (RFC 2119 best practice for English specs)"
            "modified_omite_escenario#0", "ch", "ERROR", "cap/spec.md", "MODIFIED \"Foo\" omits scenario(s) the current spec still has: \"B\". The modified block has 1 scenario; the current spec has 2 scenarios. It adds none. Copy the omitted scenarios into the MODIFIED block (a MODIFIED requirement replaces the whole block, so archive refuses to drop them)."
            "modified_tras_rename#0", "ch", "ERROR", "cap/spec.md", "MODIFIED \"B\" omits scenario(s) the current spec still has: \"S2\". The modified block has 1 scenario; the current spec has 2 scenarios. It adds none. Copy the omitted scenarios into the MODIFIED block (a MODIFIED requirement replaces the whole block, so archive refuses to drop them)."
            "modified_sin_base#0", "ch", "INFO", "cap/spec.md", "Archive would refuse this delta: cap MODIFIED failed for header \"### Requirement: Inexistente\" - not found"
            "proyecto_mixto#0", "rota", "ERROR", "requirements[0]", "Requirement \"Foo\" must contain SHALL or MUST"
            "proyecto_mixto#2", "rota", "ERROR", "requirements[0]", "Requirement \"Foo\" must contain SHALL or MUST"
            "solo_avisos#0", "cap", "WARNING", "requirements[0]", "Requirement \"Foo\" should contain SHALL or MUST (RFC 2119 best practice for English specs)"
            "solo_avisos#1", "cap", "WARNING", "requirements[0]", "Requirement \"Foo\" should contain SHALL or MUST (RFC 2119 best practice for English specs)"
    leccion:
        La medida queda fijada contra la salida real, no sólo contra evidencia fabricada.
